8,Mixtecan Family | SIL Mexico,https://mexico.sil.org/language_culture/mixtec,"The most famous collection of Mixtec artifacts was found in tomb seven at the Monte Alban archaeological site in Oaxaca. Like other Otomanguean languages, the languages in the Mixtecan family are tonal, which means that the pitch with which a word is pronounced is so important that a change in the pitch can change one word into an entirely different one.","Mixtec, Western Juxtlahuaca",Otomanguean
